.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_KEM-EC 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_KEM-EC
.Nd EVP_KEM EC keytype and algorithm support
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Sy EC
keytype and its parameters are described in
.Xr EVP_PKEY-EC 7 .
See
.Xr EVP_PKEY_encapsulate 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_decapsulate 3
for more info.
.Ss EC KEM parameters
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqoperation" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KEM_PARAM_OPERATION Ns )<UTF8 string>
The OpenSSL EC Key Encapsulation Mechanisms only supports the following
default operation (operating mode):
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqDHKEM" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KEM_PARAM_OPERATION_DHKEM )
The encapsulate function generates an ephemeral keypair.
It produces keymaterial by doing an ECDH key exchange using the
ephemeral private key and a supplied recipient public key.
A HKDF operation using the keymaterial and a kem context then produces a
shared secret.
The shared secret and the ephemeral public key are returned.
The decapsulate function uses the recipient private key and the
ephemeral public key to produce the same keymaterial, which can then be
used to produce the same shared secret.
See
.Lk https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9180.html#name-dh-based-kem-dhkem
.El
.Pp
This can be set using either
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_kem_op 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3 .
.It \(dqikme" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KEM_PARAM_IKME Ns ) <octet string>
Used to specify the key material used for generation of the ephemeral
key.
This value should not be reused for other purposes.
It can only be used for the curves "P-256", "P-384" and "P-521" and
should have a length of at least the size of the encoded private key
(i.e.
32, 48 and 66 for the listed curves).
If this value is not set, then a random ikm is used.
.El
.Sh CONFORMING TO
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It RFC9180
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_kem_op 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_encapsulate 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_decapsulate 3
.Xr EVP_KEYMGMT 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY 3 ,
.Xr provider-keymgmt 7
.Sh HISTORY
This functionality was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
.Pp
The
.Qo Li operation Qc
(operating mode) was a required parameter prior to OpenSSL 3.5. As of
OpenSSL 3.5,
.Qo Li DHKEM Qc
is the default operating mode, and no explicit value need be specified.
